"use strict";(self.webpackChunkdocs=self.webpackChunkdocs||[]).push([[2376],{17853:e=>{e.exports=JSON.parse('{"functions":[{"name":"init","desc":"Bootstrap hook. Sets up the lobby loop and the client-facing game mode data.\\n\\nGame mode modules are cloned into ReplicatedStorage so clients can read the\\nconfigs (names, descriptions, round times) needed to render vote cards \u2014 but\\neach clone\'s `Init` child is destroyed first, so the server-only round logic\\nis never replicated.\\n\\nIt then installs the Heartbeat lobby loop described on [GameService], plus a\\nhandler that catches up newly loaded players: anyone joining during an\\nintermission receives the remaining countdown and the right music cue, and\\nanyone joining an under-populated lobby is told how many more players are\\nneeded.\\n\\nThe \\"need N more players\\" hint is rate-limited to one every\\n`INSUFFICIENT_HINT_INTERVAL` seconds, except that a change in N sends\\nimmediately \u2014 so the count visibly ticks down as people join rather than\\nlagging behind.\\n\\nNo-ops entirely when the `Minigames` feature flag is off.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":114,"path":"src/Server/Features/Minigames/GameService.luau"}},{"name":"voteWrap","desc":"Runs the map/mode vote and **yields until it resolves**, returning the winning\\ncandidate or `nil` if no vote could be held.\\n\\n:::danger\\nReturns `DEBUG_GAME` immediately if that constant is set \u2014 which it currently\\nis. Everything below this line is dead until it is cleared. See [GameService].\\n:::\\n\\nBuilds a pool by filtering the registered modes down to those whose\\n`minimumPlayers` the lobby can satisfy, then drawing up to\\n`MinigameConfig.voteSlots` of them at random, each paired with a random map\\nfrom its own map list. Returns `nil` if nothing qualifies, and short-circuits\\nwithout a vote if exactly one candidate survives.\\n\\nWith a real pool it starts [VoteService], broadcasts the vote countdown, and\\nwaits on either `VoteEnded` or a `votingTime` timeout \u2014 whichever comes first,\\nwith the loser cancelled. Players who load mid-vote are folded in and given the\\n*remaining* time rather than a fresh timer, and are skipped entirely once fewer\\nthan two seconds remain.\\n\\nAfterwards it prunes voters who left, asks [VoteService] for the winner, shows\\nthe result to the surviving voters, and returns the winning candidate.","params":[],"returns":[{"desc":"The chosen mode and map","lua_type":"MinigameTypes.VotePoolItem?"}],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":304,"path":"src/Server/Features/Minigames/GameService.luau"}},{"name":"gameWrap","desc":"Runs one complete round and **yields for its entire duration**. Called by the\\nlobby loop; it sets `inProgress` on entry, and the caller clears it on return.\\n\\nChooses the round in priority order: a game a player paid to queue via\\n[MinigameService.getNextQueuedGame] wins outright, otherwise\\n[GameService.voteWrap] decides.\\n\\nIt then constructs the mode \u2014 which loads the map as a side effect of\\n[BaseGameMode.new] \u2014 records it as `activeGameMode`, and clears that reference\\nwhen the round destroys itself.\\n\\nBefore starting it waits out an estimated map load time scaled by part count\\n(see [MinigameUtil.calculateMapLoadTime]), then broadcasts the round info card\\n(mode, map, description, thumbnail, length, lives, teams) and waits four\\nseconds for players to read it.\\n\\nPlayer count is re-verified before *every* one of those waits and again after,\\nbecause each yields; a lobby that drains below the mode\'s minimum tears the\\nround down and returns rather than starting an unplayable game.\\n\\nFinally calls [BaseGameMode:Start], which yields until the round is over.","params":[],"returns":[],"function_type":"static","source":{"line":499,"path":"src/Server/Features/Minigames/GameService.luau"}}],"properties":[],"types":[],"name":"GameService","desc":"Round orchestrator for the minigame rotation. Owns the lobby loop that decides\\n*when* a round happens and *which* round it is; [BaseGameMode] owns what\\nhappens once one starts.\\n\\n### The loop\\n\\nA single Heartbeat connection, installed by [GameService.init], drives\\neverything. It idles whenever a round is live, one is being set up, or the\\nserver is empty. Otherwise:\\n\\n- **Not enough players** \u2014 reset the intermission timer and periodically hint\\n  how many more are needed. The threshold is the *lowest*\\n  `minimumPlayers` across all registered modes, so a two-player mode can start\\n  even if others need more.\\n- **Enough players** \u2014 accumulate toward `MinigameConfig.lobbyWaitTime`, then\\n  call [GameService.gameWrap], which yields for the entire round.\\n\\n`inProgress` and `activeGameMode` are what keep this re-entrant-safe: the\\nHeartbeat handler keeps firing while `gameWrap` is yielding, and both flags\\nstop it starting a second round underneath the first.\\n\\n### Picking a round\\n\\n```\\ngameWrap\\n  \u2514\u2500\u2500 a player paid to queue a game?  \u2192 use it\\n      else voteWrap\\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 build a pool of up to `voteSlots` (mode, map) candidates\\n            \u251c\u2500\u2500 one candidate only \u2192 return it, skip the vote\\n            \u2514\u2500\u2500 otherwise \u2192 VoteService, wait for the result\\n```\\n\\nOnce a candidate is chosen, `gameWrap` constructs the mode, waits out the map\\nload, shows the round info card, and calls `Start`. Player count is re-checked\\nat every one of those steps, because each yields and people leave.\\n\\n:::danger\\n`DEBUG_GAME` at the top of this module is a **hard override**. While it is a\\ntable, the truthiness test in [GameService.voteWrap] returns it before any\\npool is built \u2014 voting never runs and the same mode and map are played\\nevery round. Leave it `nil` outside of debugging.\\n:::\\n\\nGated by [FeatureFlags].Minigames \u2014 disabled by default; per-project forks\\nenable it deliberately. With the flag off `init` returns before installing the\\nHeartbeat loop, so no round ever starts.","tags":["dormant"],"realm":["Server"],"source":{"line":56,"path":"src/Server/Features/Minigames/GameService.luau"}}')}}]);